{
  "id": "LendLoopEvent001",
  "name": "LendLoop: Request notification",
  "active": false,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "event-001",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -20,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Request notification\nConvex posts here when a borrow request is created or changes status.\n\n**The HTTP response is the delivery receipt.** It is sent after Notify, so 2xx means the person was notified and anything else makes Convex retry with a new `attempt` number. Deduplicating on `eventId:attempt` drops replays while letting genuine retries through.\n\nThe mock notifier records the message in this execution's data. Swap **Notify (mock)** for an email, Slack or Discord node to send for real.",
        "width": 1500,
        "height": 190,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "event-002",
      "name": "Loan event",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "lendloop-loan-event",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {
          "rawBody": true
        }
      },
      "webhookId": "lendloop-loan-event"
    },
    {
      "id": "event-003",
      "name": "Read signature",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        260,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const { headers } = $input.first().json;\n\nlet rawBody = '';\ntry {\n  rawBody = (await this.helpers.getBinaryDataBuffer(0, 'data')).toString('utf8');\n} catch {\n  // An empty request has no binary part. It fails verification below.\n}\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    timestamp: headers['x-ll-timestamp'] ?? '',\n    signature: headers['x-ll-signature'] ?? '',\n    rawBody,\n  },\n}];"
      }
    },
    {
